<h1>[@label_help]</h1>
The current section is a helping guide to use [@label_product].
<br />
<h4>Sign in as existing user</h4>
When not logged in, the main menu provides the option to sign in. The email adress and password are required to sign in.
<h4>Register a new user</h4>
When not logged in, the main menu provides the option to register a new user. The user must provide a valid email and agree to the terms of service, as weel as the privacy policy. A random password will be generated and sent to his email address. The password may be changed later from the account menu when logged in.
<h4>Recover forgotten password</h4>
When not logged in, the sign in menu option provides the opportunity to recover a forgotten password. The user by pressing the Recover Password button, provides the email address in order to generate a new random password. The password will be sent to his email address. If access to the originally used email address is not available, please contact us to resolve the issue.
<h4>Account</h4>
The account section represent core properties of the business. All information in the current section is optional. However, the preferences section contain factors that affect further automation in creating appopintments for faster results.
<h4>Account - Business</h4>
The current section is completely optional and the purpose is to provide information for future platform automations such as running bulk campaigns. The user may provide the brand name of the business, the VIES or tax number, the Address, the Phone number, the Cell phone and the business Owner name.
<h4>Account - Preferences</h4>
The current section is completely optional but has an impact in using the application, in terms of automation. It is advised for the user to type in the appropriate information to their business.
<ul>
	<li>The Number of employees including the owner, corresponds to the number of employees that may complete and appointment. This number may not be below 1, as it includes the working owner of the business. The platform calculates all overlapping appointments. In case that there is not any free employee to serve, a message is displayed that advises the user to change the appointment time.</li>
	<li>The Duration field is the generic length of each appointment, by default 30 minutes. This may be changed when adding a new appointment.</li>
	<li>The Opening and Closing are the feault operating time interval for the business. This may be changed when adding a new appointment.</li>
</ul>
<h4>Account - Password change</h4>
To change the password, the old password must be provided for verification, as well as the new desired password.
<h4>Account - Delete user</h4>
By providing the current user password for verification, the user will be deleted, all information regarding the user will be deleted from the database, and the user will be immediately signed out.
<h4>Calendar</h4>
On the calendar view all days of the month are presented. If there are appointments for a specific day, the day appears with the number of the day appointments below.
<ul>
	<li>Four buttons appear on the top, in order to navigate between months and years.</li>
	<li>By selecting a specific day, the user may overview the day appointments.</li>
	<li>From the today button, the user can overview the appointments assigned today. There is a button to add a new appointment.</li>
	<li>There is an option to fast search for a specific appointment by description or customer at the bottom of the calendar view.</li>
	<li>The number of employees including the owner appear on the bottom with an option to alter the number of employees.</li>
</ul>
<h4>Appointments and Events</h4>
On the top, the total number of day appointments appear. Four buttons appear on the top, in order to navigate between days and weeks. The user may return to the caldendar view or add a new appointment.
<br />
Each appointment is presented in a timely order, including the duration, customer and description. The contact information of each customer is processed, detecting either emails or phone numbers.
<br />
A notification that the system is unable to serve due to lack of employees and overlapping appers, in cases that more overlapping appointments appear than the total number of employees that can support an appointment
<h4>Availability</h4>
The availability section presents a timeline of appointment free ranges, based on the stored appointments, the opening hours, and the closing hours of the business.
<br />
An Overlap notification appears on a specific time range, to notify the user that an active appointment is set during this time range.
<br />
The user may add a new appointment in the available time ranges.
<h4>Add appointment</h4>
By adding a new appointment, the user sets the appointment specifications, including the date, the starting time, the duration, the customer, the contact information and the appointment description.
<h4>Edit appointment</h4>
The pencil button appear in each appointment. The user may alter any appointment specification, including the date, the starting time, the duration, the customer, the contact information and the appointment description.
<h4>Delete appointment</h4>
The X button appear in each appointment. The user cancels the selected appointment, and free time is allocated in the availability section, to store new appointments. The deleted appointment is calculated as a cancelled appointment.
<h4>Export appointment</h4>
The paperclip icon appear in each appointment. This fucntion exports the selected appointment to .ics format (iCalendar), a plain-text standard for storing and exchanging calendar information, such as events, tasks, and meeting details, across platforms like Outlook, Google Calendar, and Apple Calendar.
<h4>Customers</h4>
A list of customers is presented based on the past appointments, including their contact information. The customer list can be sorted ascending or descending based on the customer name or contact information. A search option is included in the top of the page to search form specific customers. The contact information of each customer is processed, detecting either emails or phone numbers.
<h4>Campaigns</h4>
The Campaign section from the main menu provides a list of all customer email addresses and phone numbers. These can be copied to other applications or use each button for bulk sending emails from an email application installed, or bulk messages from a mobile phone.
<h4>Statistics</h4>
The Statistics section contains useful information about all appointments up to today, customers including the most and least frequent (including their contact information), the current application as well as the server installed.
<h4>Contact</h4>
In any case, use the contact email from the menu to contact us for resolving any issues, questions, suggestions etc.<br />
<h4>Terms</h4>
Please review the terms thouroughly in the Terms menu section, before using [@label_product].
